  - target: term/bereavement-benefit-regime
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source explicitly sends later deaths to chapter 63, while allowing retained earlier awards
      to be considered in their own regime.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch58/0003
      quote: "58001   This Chapter gives brief guidance on Widow’s Benefits (WMA and WP) that have\n        been
        replaced by BB where the late spouse died on or after 9.4.011. Detailed\n        guidance on BB can be found
        in DMG Chapter 63.\n                                                                                 1 WRP
        Act 99"
      locator: DMG 58001
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch63/0001
      quote: "63002 No new claims for WB were accepted in respect of deaths on or after 9.4.01. People already\n\
        receiving WB on that date can continue to receive it for as long as the qualifying conditions apply (see\n\
        DMG Chapter 58)."
      locator: DMG 63002
  - target: term/wma-child-benefit-evidence
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Outside pregnancy cases the chapter makes WMA dependent on Child Benefit entitlement and seeks
      HMRC evidence.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch58/0007
      quote: "58203   WMA (except pregnancy cases) and the increase of WMA for a child depend on the\n        claimant
        being entitled to CHB. Decisions on entitlement to CHB are now given by\n        HMRC. DMs should seek evidence
        from HMRC about entitlement to CHB.\n\n\n        Treating as entitled to child benefit where married more\n\
        \        than once"
      locator: DMG 58203
